Recommends: gstreamer1.0-vaapi
Description: Miracast server (sink) for Ubuntu
 Ubuntu Miracast Server is a desktop application that acts as a
 Miracast sink — receiving wireless screen casts from Miracast
 source devices over Wi-Fi Direct.
 .
 This is a Rust port of the original Python/PyGObject application,
 preserving identical functional and non-functional behaviour.
 .
 Features:
  * Receive Miracast wireless display streams
  * Automatic device discovery via Wi-Fi Direct P2P
  * Hardware-accelerated video decoding (VAAPI/NVDEC)
  * Audio support (AAC)
  * Session history tracking
  * Optional headless systemd user service mode
  * GTK 4 / libadwaita user interface
